<Document>
<name>London: Bridge to Bridge (5.3 mi)</name>
<description>DRAFT route. Not an official Nike route. Check it on the ground before you rely on it.</description>
<Style id="route"><LineStyle><color>ff2b39c0</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Placemark><name>London: Bridge to Bridge (5.3 mi)</name><styleUrl>#route</styleUrl>
<LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-0.0985,51.5081,0 -0.1043,51.5083,0 -0.1085,51.5084,0 -0.1105,51.508,0 -0.114,51.5075,0 -0.116,51.5068,0 -0.119,51.506,0 -0.1196,51.5033,0 -0.1195,51.502,0 -0.1196,51.5008,0 -0.1238,51.501,0 -0.1236,51.502,0 -0.122,51.507,0 -0.1203,51.5085,0 -0.1175,51.51,0 -0.114,51.5108,0 -0.1045,51.511,0 -0.0985,51.5102,0 -0.094,51.5096,0 -0.0905,51.5092,0 -0.0875,51.509,0 -0.084,51.5087,0 -0.079,51.5076,0 -0.0748,51.5072,0 -0.0762,51.504,0 -0.079,51.505,0 -0.0815,51.5063,0 -0.084,51.5062,0 -0.088,51.5064,0 -0.0898,51.5062,0 -0.0905,51.507,0 -0.094,51.5077,0 -0.097,51.5081,0 -0.0985,51.5081,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Folder><name>Landmarks</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Tate Modern</name><description>Start and finish. The old Bankside Power Station, now a free modern art museum. The crew meets on the riverside terrace.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0985,51.5081,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. London Eye</name><description>The 135-metre observation wheel. The path narrows here, so run single file past the queue.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1196,51.5033,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Westminster Bridge</name><description>The first crossing. Big Ben and the Houses of Parliament are straight ahead as you run over.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1217,51.5009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Cleopatra&#x27;s Needle</name><description>An ancient Egyptian obelisk on Victoria Embankment, guarded by two bronze sphinxes.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1203,51.5085,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Somerset House</name><description>The long neoclassical river front above the Embankment. Roughly the halfway point of the 5K.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.114,51.5108,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Millennium Bridge</name><description>The 5K turns onto this footbridge and runs straight back to Tate Modern. St Paul&#x27;s dome is right behind you.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0985,51.5102,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Tower of London</name><description>Nearly a thousand years old. The riverside walk runs between the fortress wall and the Thames.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.079,51.5076,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Tower Bridge</name><description>The far turn. Climb the steps, cross between the towers and drop down to the south bank.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0755,51.5056,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. HMS Belfast</name><description>A Second World War cruiser moored on the south bank, now a museum ship.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0815,51.5063,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. Borough Market</name><description>One of London&#x27;s oldest food markets. The last mile starts here.</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0898,51.5062,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
